findings:
- finding_id: C1
  title: from_file_or_default swallows ALL errors including parse and permission failures
  weight: 8
  phase_ideal: dev
  caught: false
  caught_by: null
  evidence: No phase identified that from_file_or_default swallows all errors. TEA
    config tests exist but none specifically test that parse/permission errors are
    distinguished from NotFound. Reviewer did not flag this.
- finding_id: I1
  title: CliError Display leaks internal details to stderr (CWE-209)
  weight: 5
  phase_ideal: reviewer
  caught: true
  caught_by: reviewer
  evidence: "Reviewer flagged '[HIGH] NotFound Display leaks raw server response body\
    \ \u2014 CWE-209 at error.rs:12' noting raw HTTP body leaks to operators. TEA\
    \ also wrote CWE-209 security tests, but the specific CliError Display leak to\
    \ stderr was partially caught \u2014 the NotFound variant leak was flagged by\
    \ reviewer, though the broader eprintln!('error: {e}') pattern was not explicitly\
    \ called out."
- finding_id: I2
  title: "SiemClient.tenant_id uses raw String \u2014 header injection risk (CWE-113)"
  weight: 5
  phase_ideal: tea
  caught: true
  caught_by: tea
  evidence: "TEA wrote CWE-113 header injection tests for tenant ID values (CR, LF,\
    \ CRLF, null bytes rejected). Dev implemented header injection prevention in client.rs:65-71.\
    \ However, the deeper issue of using raw String instead of TenantId from axiathon-core\
    \ was not flagged \u2014 only the injection vector was mitigated."
- finding_id: I3
  title: Dependencies use direct version strings instead of workspace = true
  weight: 3
  phase_ideal: dev
  caught: false
  caught_by: null
  evidence: No phase flagged that dependencies use direct version strings instead
    of workspace = true. Reviewer noted a toml version mismatch but did not flag the
    broader workspace dependency pattern issue.
- finding_id: I4
  title: "Config token field silently ignored \u2014 secret left on disk"
  weight: 5
  phase_ideal: reviewer
  caught: true
  caught_by: reviewer
  evidence: "Reviewer flagged '[MEDIUM] serde(flatten) silently absorbs config typos\
    \ at config.rs:15' \u2014 noting typos are silently absorbed into _extra with\
    \ no warning. Recommended #[serde(deny_unknown_fields)] or logging warnings. This\
    \ directly addresses the config token field silently ignored issue."
- finding_id: I5
  title: "Vacuously true test \u2014 assertion is None || true"
  weight: 5
  phase_ideal: tea
  caught: false
  caught_by: null
  evidence: No phase identified the vacuously true assertion pattern (is_none() ||
    ...). TEA wrote config tests but the specific assert!(config.server().is_none()
    || ...) pattern was not flagged by any phase.
- finding_id: I6
  title: "Test with zero assertions \u2014 only checks non-panic"
  weight: 5
  phase_ideal: tea
  caught: false
  caught_by: null
  evidence: No phase identified the zero-assertion test that only checks non-panic.
    TEA wrote config tests but did not flag that 'let _ = config;' has no meaningful
    assertions.
